# Chinese Text Encoding Safety

This project serves Chinese users. For code involving LLM prompts, string processing, and text persistence, always preserve Chinese characters end-to-end.

## Required Practices

- Use UTF-8 explicitly for file I/O (`encoding="utf-8"`).
- Serialize JSON with `ensure_ascii=False` to keep readable Chinese text.
- Keep storage and transport layers Unicode-safe (e.g., DB collation/charset supports Chinese such as `utf8mb4`).
- Avoid transformations that can corrupt characters (incorrect encoding decode/encode cycles).

## Examples

```python
# ❌ BAD: may escape Chinese, harder to debug/review
with open("prompt.json", "w") as f:
    json.dump({"prompt": "请总结以下内容"}, f)

# ✅ GOOD: preserve readable Chinese characters
with open("prompt.json", "w", encoding="utf-8") as f:
    json.dump({"prompt": "请总结以下内容"}, f, ensure_ascii=False)
```

```python
# ❌ BAD: platform-default encoding can cause corruption
text = open("template.txt").read()

# ✅ GOOD: explicit UTF-8 decode
text = open("template.txt", encoding="utf-8").read()
```
